{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01_E06ZcQ5mhJNivPAfpRXK0435","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"grep -rn 'agents' /home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -40"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:354:Fired before pi decides whether to trust a project with dynamic configs (`.pi` or `.agents/skills`). It runs during startup and when session replacement (for example `/resume`) enters a cwd whose trust has not been resolved in the current process. Only user/global extensions and CLI `-e` extensions participate; project-local extensions are not loaded until after trust is resolved.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:2970:| `subagent/` | Spawn sub-agents | `registerTool`, `exec` |\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:11:- Build custom tools that spawn sub-agents\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:348:  - `.agents/skills/` in `cwd` and ancestor directories (up to git repo root, or filesystem root when not in a repo)\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:357:  - `~/.agents/skills/`\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:696:  agentsFilesOverride: (current) => ({\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:697:    agentsFiles: [\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:698:      ...current.agentsFiles,\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:914:const contextFiles = loader.getAgentsFiles().agentsFiles;\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/security.md:14:- project `.agents/skills` in the current directory or an ancestor directory\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/settings.md:14:On interactive startup, pi asks before trusting a project folder that contains project-local settings, resources, or project `.agents/skills` and has no saved decision for the folder or a parent folder in `~/.pi/agent/trust.json`. Trusting a project allows pi to load `.pi/settings.json` and `.pi` resources, install missing project packages, and execute project extensions.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/skills.md:7:Pi implements the [Agent Skills standard](https://agentskills.io/specification), warning about most violations but remaining lenient. Pi allows skill names to differ from their parent directory even though the standard disallows it; that rule is suboptimal for shared skill directories used across multiple agent harnesses.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/skills.md:28:  - `~/.agents/skills/`\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/skills.md:31:  - `.agents/skills/` in `cwd` and ancestor directories (up to git repo root, or filesystem root when not in a repo)\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/skills.md:39:- In `~/.agents/skills/` and project `.agents/skills/`, root `.md` files are ignored\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/skills.md:67:2. The system prompt includes available skills in XML format per the [specification](https://agentskills.io/integrate-skills)\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/skills.md:139:Per the [Agent Skills specification](https://agentskills.io/specification#frontmatter-required):\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/usage.md:121:On interactive startup, pi asks before trusting a project folder that contains project-local settings, resources, or project `.agents/skills` and has no saved decision for the folder or a parent folder in `~/.pi/agent/trust.json`. Trusting a project allows pi to load `.pi/settings.json` and `.pi` resources, install missing project packages, and execute project extensions.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/usage.md:303:It intentionally does not include built-in MCP, sub-agents, permission popups, plan mode, to-dos, or background bash. You can build or install those workflows as extensions or packages, or use external tools such as containers and tmux.\n"}],"details":{}}}
