{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I understand the discovery entry: `~/.pi/agent/agents/**/*.md` — user scope. For rick, since it injects `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=~/.rick/pi/agent`, the agent dir is `~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/**/*.md`.\n\nBut wait, the task says `runtime.AgentDir()/agents/{think,research,exporter}.md`. And `runtime.AgentDir()` returns `~/.rick/pi/agent` (or `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR`). So the agent files go in `AgentDir()/agents/`.\n\nNow I understand the requirements clearly. Let me now understand:\n1. The current env module: `DeployRickCustomizations()` already exists in `customizations.go`, handling rick-gates hook + rick skills.\n2. I need to add agent registration to it (or a new function called by it).\n\nThe task says: \"此任务产出的是 env 职责 3（`DeployRickCustomizations`）中「agent」定制物的具体内容\" and \"由 env 职责 3 幂等写入\".\n\nSo I need to modify `DeployRickCustomizations()` (or add a helper called by it) to write the 3 agent files.\n\nKey requirements:\n1. Write `AgentDir()/agents/{think,research,exporter}.md`\n2. frontmatter contains `name`/`description`/`tools`/`defaultContext` + `rick-managed: true`\n3. system prompt = corresponding skill wiki content (non-empty, contains skill marker)\n4. Idempotent + overwrite semantics:\n   - Only overwrite files with `rick-managed: true` in frontmatter\n   - Skip files without `rick-managed: true`\n   - Repeated runs don't duplicate\n5. tools align with pi tool names (read, grep, find, ls, bash, web_search, fetch_content, write)\n\nLet me look at the source of the skill wiki content. The task says:\n- think.md system prompt = `templates/skills/think.md`\n- research.md = `templates/skills/research.md`\n- exporter.md = `templates/skills/exporter.md`\n\nThese are in `internal/prompt/templates/skills/`. Let me check how they're embedded/accessed. The builder's templates are go embed. Let me check the pibuilder and how templates are embedded.\n\nLet me check the embed structure."}}
