{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The test fails as expected (RED state confirmed). Now let me implement the GREEN phase.\n\nLet me write the implementation. I'll modify:\n1. `internal/env/customizations.go` — add agent deployment.\n2. `internal/env/check.go` — update `requiredRickAgents` and fix `CheckRickAgents` to check `.md` files.\n3. `internal/env/env_test.go` — update tests.\n4. Possibly add a helper to `internal/prompt/manager.go` for single skill loading (or use `LoadCoreSkills`).\n\nLet me decide on the approach for accessing skill content. I'll use `prompt.LoadCoreSkills([]string{name})`. This is already exported. Let me verify it works for single name.\n\nActually, I realize there might be a cleaner approach: I can add a new exported function `LoadCoreSkill(name string) string` that returns the raw content of a single skill without the log warning behavior. But `LoadCoreSkills` already works. Let me just use `LoadCoreSkills([]string{name})`.\n\nWait, actually, let me reconsider the import. `internal/env` currently imports `internal/runtime` and `internal/workspace`. Adding `internal/prompt` import. Let me double-check there's no cycle by building after the change.\n\nLet me now write the code.\n\nFirst, the agent definition. Let me design a struct and a list:\n\n```go\n// rickAgentSpec 描述一个 rick 自定义 agent 的 frontmatter + system prompt 来源。\ntype rickAgentSpec struct {\n\tname            string\n\tdescription     string\n\ttools           string // 逗号分隔的 pi 工具名\n\tdefaultContext  string\n\tskillName       string // templates/skills/{skillName}.md 的 system prompt 来源\n}\n```\n\nActually, `skillName` == `name` for all three (think/research/exporter). So I can derive it. But to be explicit and future-proof, I'll keep a `skillName` field. Actually, they're identical, so I'll just use `name` as the skill name.\n\nLet me write the agent specs:\n\n```go\nvar rickAgents = []rickAgentSpec{\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"think\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"推理过程分析 + 4 维风险评估 + 启发性 3 问方法论（SENSE S2/EC）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, grep, find, ls\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"research\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"尽调树 + 信源加权方法论（澄清事实模糊性到极限）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, grep, find, ls, bash, web_search, fetch_content\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"exporter\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"RFC 输出方法论（大纲 + 内容两阶段固化）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, write, bash\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n}\n```\n\nNow the frontmatter generation:\n\n```go\nfunc renderAgentFile(spec rickAgentSpec) (string, error) {\n\tbody := prompt.LoadCoreSkills([]string{spec.name})\n\tif body == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"embedded skill %q not found for agent %q\", spec.name, spec.name)\n\t}\n\tfm := fmt.Sprintf(`---\nname: %s\ndescription: %s\ntools: %s\ndefaultContext: %s\nsystemPromptMode: replace\nrick-managed: true\n---\n\n`, spec.name, spec.description, spec.tools, spec.defaultContext)\n\treturn fm + body, nil\n}\n```\n\nWait, I need to be careful about the trailing. The body should start right after the `---` closing line. The test's parse_frontmatter:\n- first line `---`\n- find next line that strips to `---`\n- body = lines after that joined.\n\nSo my file should be:\n```\n---\nname: think\n...\nrick-managed: true\n---\n<body>\n```\n\nThe body is the skill content, which starts with `# skill:think(...)`. So body non-empty.\n\nNote: the body (skill content) itself contains `---` horizontal rules (e.g., think.md has `---` separators). But those are AFTER the closing `---` of the frontmatter, so parse_frontmatter correctly treats them as body (it only finds the FIRST `---` after line 0 as the closing). Wait, let me re-check parse_frontmatter:\n\n```python\nend = None\nfor i in range(1, len(lines)):\n    if lines[i].strip() == '---':\n        end = i\n        break\n```\n\nSo it finds the FIRST line (after index 0) that strips to `---`. My frontmatter is:\n```\n---          (index 0)\nname: think  (index 1)\ndescription: ...\ntools: ...\ndefaultContext: ...\nsystemPromptMode: replace\nrick-managed: true\n---          (index 6) ← closing\n# skill:think(...)  (body)\n...\n```\n\nGood, the closing `---` is at index 6, which is found. Body = everything after. Good.\n\nBut wait, I should double check: the think.md skill content has `---` lines like:\n```\n---\n\n## think pipeline\n```\nYes, but those are in the body, after the frontmatter closing `---`. So parse_frontmatter only finds the frontmatter closing `---` (first one after index 0). \n\nNow, there's a subtle issue: what if the skill content itself starts with `---`? Let me check think.md starts with `# skill:think(...)`. research.md starts with `# skill:research（...）`. exporter.md starts with `# skill:exporter（...）`. None start with `---`. Good.\n\nNow the overwrite check and write:\n\n```go\nfunc deployRickAgents() error {\n\tagentsDir := filepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"agents\")\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(agentsDir, 0755); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"create agents dir: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tfor _, spec := range rickAgents {\n\t\tif err := deployRickAgent(agentsDir, spec); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc deployRickAgent(agentsDir string, spec rickAgentSpec) error {\n\ttarget := filepath.Join(agentsDir, spec.name+\".md\")\n\t// 覆盖判定：仅覆盖 rick 标记文件（或不存在），无标记跳过。\n\tif data, err := os.ReadFile(target); err == nil {\n\t\tif !hasRickManagedMarker(string(data)) {\n\t\t\treturn nil // 用户自定义文件，不覆盖。\n\t\t}\n\t} else if !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", target, err)\n\t}\n\n\tcontent, err := renderAgentFile(spec)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(target, []byte(content), 0644); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write agent %s: %w\", spec.name, err)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n```\n\nAnd the marker check:\n\n```go\nfunc hasRickManagedMarker(content string) bool {\n\tlines := strings.Split(content, \"\\n\")\n\tif len(lines) == 0 || strings.TrimSpace(lines[0]) != \"---\" {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfor _, ln := range lines[1:] {\n\t\ttrimmed := strings.TrimSpace(ln)\n\t\tif trimmed == \"---\" {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t\tif trimmed == \"rick-managed: true\" {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n```\n\nNow, I need to add `strings` and `internal/prompt` imports to customizations.go.\n\nLet me also think about the `DeployRickCustomizations` update:\n\n```go\nfunc DeployRickCustomizations() error {\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"locate rick dir: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := deployRickCustomizations(filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\")); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\treturn deployRickAgents()\n}\n```\n\nNow for check.go:\n```go\nvar requiredRickAgents = []string{\"think\", \"research\", \"exporter\"}\n\nfunc CheckRickAgents() []string {\n\tvar missing []string\n\tfor _, name := range requiredRickAgents {\n\t\tif !runtime.FileExists(filepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"agents\", name+\".md\")) {\n\t\t\tmissing = append(missing, name)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn missing\n}\n```\n\nNow the tests. Let me update `env_test.go`:\n\n1. `TestDeployRickCustomizations` — currently calls `deployRickCustomizations(src)` directly. I should keep that test for skills deployment, but maybe add agent deployment tests. Actually, let me add a new test `TestDeployRickAgents` that covers:\n   - normal: 3 files with correct frontmatter + non-empty body + skill marker\n   - idempotent: run twice, content unchanged\n   - overwrite semantics: no-marker file skipped; marker file overwritten\n\nActually, since `deployRickAgents` uses embedded content (not `src`), it doesn't need `src`. Let me write a focused test.\n\n2. `TestCheckRickAgents_NoRequiredAgents` → rename to `TestCheckRickAgents_Missing` and check it returns 3 missing when nothing deployed. Or