{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Only env_test.go references these. Good. Also there's `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam` which calls `pi.DeployCustomizations()` after `os.Chdir(empty)`. This now calls the full `DeployRickCustomizations()` which calls `deployRickCustomizations(empty/.rick/skills)` (returns nil since no skills dir) AND `deployRickAgents()` (writes agents to `$HOME/.rick/pi/agent/agents/` where HOME is temp). That's fine, it will write agents to temp HOME. The test only checks no error. Good.\n\nWait, let me re-read `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam`:\n```go\nfunc TestRuntimeEnv_Seam(t *testing.T) {\n\tvar _ RuntimeEnv = NewPiEnv()\n\tpi := NewPiEnv()\n\n\torig, err := os.Getwd()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tempty := t.TempDir()\n\tif err := os.Chdir(empty); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tdefer func() { _ = os.Chdir(orig) }()\n\tt.Setenv(\"HOME\", t.TempDir())\n\n\tif err := pi.DeployCustomizations(); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"DeployCustomizations should be tolerant, got %v\", err)\n\t}\n\t_ = pi.CheckReady()\n}\n```\n\nAfter chdir to `empty` (a temp dir), `workspace.GetRickDir()` returns `empty/.rick`. `deployRickCustomizations(empty/.rick/skills)` → skills dir doesn't exist → returns nil. Then `deployRickAgents()` → writes to `$HOME/.rick/pi/agent/agents/`. This works fine. Good.\n\nBut wait, there's a subtlety: `os.Chdir` affects the whole test process. Since Go tests run sequentially in the same package (unless t.Parallel), and this test has `defer os.Chdir(orig)`, it should be fine. It's an existing pattern.\n\nNow let me implement everything.\n\nLet me write the new file `internal/env/agents.go`, then edit `customizations.go` and `check.go` and `env_test.go`.\n\nLet me start writing."}}
