{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"So the `doing_check` requires:\n1. tasks.json parseable ✓\n2. debug/ directory check — if `debug/` doesn't exist, returns nil (fine). No debug.md file in doing/ root is checked. Wait, the `tools_doing_check.go` doc says \"debug.md exists (mandatory work log)\" but the actual code `RunDoingCheck` only checks `debug/` directory and `tasks.json`. The `runDoingCheck` in `tools_doing_check.go` calls `executor.RunDoingCheck` (which checks debug/ dir), then LoadTasksJSON and checks:\n   - no \"running\" zombie tasks\n   - no \"success\" tasks with empty commit_hash\n\nSo actually the \"debug.md mandatory\" is NOT in the current code — it's only in the doc comment. The actual check is: tasks.json parseable + debug/ dir format (optional) + no running zombie + success tasks have commit_hash.\n\nWait, but there's no `debug/` directory in `.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/`. That's fine (CheckDebugDir returns nil if no debug dir).\n\nSo for doing_check to pass for task9:\n1. task9 must NOT be \"running\" (zombie) — must be \"success\" or \"failed\".\n2. If task9 is \"success\", it needs commit_hash.\n3. No other tasks in \"running\" state.\n\nCurrently tasks.json has task9 = \"running\". So I need to:\n1. Commit my code changes.\n2. Update tasks.json: task9 → \"success\" with commit_hash = my commit hash.\n\nBut wait — is there a mechanism that auto-marks task success? Let me check the `mark-task-success` skill or the executor's tasks_json. Actually, the task9_doing_prompt says \"check pass 后才算完成\". And the Doing Loop COMMIT step says: commit, then run doing_check. But doing_check needs task9 to be \"success\" with commit_hash. \n\nLet me look at how the previous tasks (task6 etc.) marked themselves success. Let me check the tasks_json.go for a mark function, and look at whether there's a `rick tools` command to mark success.\n\nActually, let me check `internal/executor/tasks_json.go`."}}
