8bb0\\uff09\\u573a\\u666f\\u4e0b exporter.md \\u672a\\u843d\\u76d8\", \"\\u542b rick-managed: true \\u7684 research.md \\u672a\\u88ab\\u8986\\u76d6\\uff08\\u5e94\\u8986\\u76d6\\uff09\", \"\\u5f02\\u5e38\\u9636\\u6bb5 think.md \\u672a\\u843d\\u76d8\", \"\\u5f02\\u5e38\\u9636\\u6bb5 research.md \\u672a\\u843d\\u76d8\", \"\\u5f02\\u5e38\\u9636\\u6bb5 exporter.md \\u672a\\u843d\\u76d8\"]}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786908774487},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test fails as expected (RED state confirmed). Now let me implement the GREEN phase.\n\nLet me write the implementation. I'll modify:\n1. `internal/env/customizations.go` — add agent deployment.\n2. `internal/env/check.go` — update `requiredRickAgents` and fix `CheckRickAgents` to check `.md` files.\n3. `internal/env/env_test.go` — update tests.\n4. Possibly add a helper to `internal/prompt/manager.go` for single skill loading (or use `LoadCoreSkills`).\n\nLet me decide on the approach for accessing skill content. I'll use `prompt.LoadCoreSkills([]string{name})`. This is already exported. Let me verify it works for single name.\n\nActually, I realize there might be a cleaner approach: I can add a new exported function `LoadCoreSkill(name string) string` that returns the raw content of a single skill without the log warning behavior. But `LoadCoreSkills` already works. Let me just use `LoadCoreSkills([]string{name})`.\n\nWait, actually, let me reconsider the import. `internal/env` currently imports `internal/runtime` and `internal/workspace`. Adding `internal/prompt` import. Let me double-check there's no cycle by building after the change.\n\nLet me now write the code.\n\nFirst, the agent definition. Let me design a struct and a list:\n\n```go\n// rickAgentSpec 描述一个 rick 自定义 agent 的 frontmatter + system prompt 来源。\ntype rickAgentSpec struct {\n\tname            string\n\tdescription     string\n\ttools           string // 逗号分隔的 pi 工具名\n\tdefaultContext  string\n\tskillName       string // templates/skills/{skillName}.md 的 system prompt 来源\n}\n```\n\nActually, `skillName` == `name` for all three (think/research/exporter). So I can derive it. But to be explicit and future-proof, I'll keep a `skillName` field. Actually, they're identical, so I'll just use `name` as the skill name.\n\nLet me write the agent specs:\n\n```go\nvar rickAgents = []rickAgentSpec{\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"think\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"推理过程分析 + 4 维风险评估 + 启发性 3 问方法论（SENSE S2/EC）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, grep, find, ls\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"research\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"尽调树 + 信源加权方法论（澄清事实模糊性到极限）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, grep, find, ls, bash, web_search, fetch_content\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"exporter\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"RFC 输出方法论（大纲 + 内容两阶段固化）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, write, bash\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n}\n```\n\nNow the frontmatter generation:\n\n```go\nfunc renderAgentFile(spec rickAgentSpec) (string, error) {\n\tbody := prompt.LoadCoreSkills([]string{spec.name})\n\tif body == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"embedded skill %q not found for agent %q\", spec.name, spec.name)\n\t}\n\tfm := fmt.Sprintf(`---\nname: %s\ndescription: %s\ntools: %s\ndefaultContext: %s\nsystemPromptMode: replace\nrick-managed: true\n---\n\n`, spec.name, spec.description, spec.tools, spec.defaultContext)\n\treturn fm + body, nil\n}\n```\n\nWait, I need to be careful about the trailing. The body should start right after the `---` closing line. The test's parse_frontmatter:\n- first line `---`\n- find next line that strips to `---`\n- body = lines after that joined.\n\nSo my file should be:\n```\n---\nname: think\n...\nrick-managed: true\n---\n<body>\n```\n\nThe body is the skill content, which starts with `# skill:think(...)`. So body non-empty.\n\nNote: the body (skill content) itself contains `---` horizontal rules (e.g., think.md has `---`